  "question": "Can repairing an existing base-count near miss before testing larger cut counts preserve more time for curve refinement?",
  "difference": "Try near-miss and retained alternate refinement at the current cut counts first. Only a successful base-count retry skips the other count hypotheses. Ordinary immediately valid base grids still search all hypotheses. Cache retries so failed base refinements are not repeated. Final acceptance remains unchanged.",
